it's time to talk with our friend monica  jackson monica good morning to you hey  good morning guys y'all look so pretty  and you're black and silver we are ready  y'all like ken and barbie this morning  we're just trying to be as stylish as  you monica oh well god bless you my  friend thank you thank you so much all  right kids hey this is so much fun and  i'm pumped to bring this to you it's  called positively arts and it's a  non-profit in the valley that helps kids  build confidence through the theater now  in today's mondays with monica segment i  had the chance to interview the founder  who bridged the gap between students and  the strip  tell us first of all your background and  why you are like  majorly qualified to do this job  oh majorly well thank you yeah i'm like  a cat i have nine lives before the age  of 45. so let's see um  my dream as a kid was to be like my dad  and be a doctor so i was on that trek  pre-med  and then a little monkey wrench i got a  call from the mouse the rat disney  right after i graduated college and they  said would you like to come and be very  good friends with pocahontas and i said  yes didn't even think about it so i left  my dream of med school and i went to  sing for the mouse for about seven years  and it was just wonderful  entering the performing arts world but i  did i missed academia so  i actually went back for my masters and  i got a masters in education with a  focus on the arts and child development  and that degree brought me to las vegas  and i actually started at the public  education foundation here in las vegas  working directly with schools and it was  then that i realized that there was a  need for arts integration and more arts  programming here in the valley so  that's when i decided to start  positively arts i left left the public  ed foundation and created a program  that specifically dealt with  enriching arts programs here in the  valley for our students very good okay  let's get into it give us the details  about positively arts because i had  never heard about it i thought i'd  interviewed everybody in las vegas so  i'm anxious for parents teachers and you  know uh people who are organizers for  like boys town and and uh boys and girls  club these are people who really need to  know you exist so that they can plug  into what you're doing even you know our  teachers at ccsd  yes and thank you so much for  sharing about our organization because  we did start in 2014 is when we became a  501c3 charity so we're a local arts  non-profit and we use the arts to  empower kids for life and one way we do  that is we use arts therapy as a way to  heal students who are undergoing any  kind of physical social or emotional  trauma and we use the performing arts as  a way to empower and build confidence  and resilience in those kids very cool  and we were talking about the teachers  or the mentors that you have on board to  help these kids get through it this is  the part i absolutely love because  you're doing some things that are you  know tough for a lot of organizations to  really clamp down on it's hard to get  into those trenches tell everybody why  your mentors are so very unique  yeah well i feel like i had a secret  back door into this world because i came  here also as a performer i couldn't give  it up so even though i was working for  the public ed foundation i went ahead  and joined some equity shows here on the  strip so now i'm friends with all of the  headliners on the strip all the  performers on the strip and one day i  turned to my cast and i said hey guys  there's all these kids here in las vegas  and we're all these professionals and i  want to create a program that bridges  the gap between the professional  performers on the strip and the local  kids in the valley and i did just that  so all of the teachers at positively  arts are the professionals that you buy  tickets and pay hundreds of dollars to  see on the strip and your kid gets to  work with them for free if you can't  afford it because that's what we're all  about we provide opportunities  regardless of your ability to pay  and see that's the part i really love  you know we go to these shows and you  know everything about vegas you're the  performer you've been up and down the  las vegas strip everything is over the  top so when you see all that decadence  children tend to think you know i'll  never get that you know that's  untouchable the fact that you bring  these people in face to face up close  and personal with these kiddos i mean it  just warms my heart and i know for as a  parent i know other parents can relate  to that and teachers as well so what  kind of reactions do you get from uh the  kiddos  i love that you say i'm a parent as well  and yes even before i moved here yeah  they were untouchable they were the  stars on the strip so yeah now creating  a program where i don't want to make it  this untouchable thing because kids have  dreams to do what we're doing on this  job and i wanted to make that in  actuality and i wanted to empower these  kids and make them believe that they can  do anything not just in the performing  arts world but in every aspect of their  life because once you have that  confidence you can do anything and the  parents love it yes okay polita if  somebody wants to get their kid involved  if a parent needs to reach out to you or  a teacher needs to connect you because  again you're you're dealing with kids  who've been through some sort of trauma  as well as mainstream kids so how do  they get in touch with you what is the  process  super simple go to our website  positivelyarts.org  if you click contact us you can contact  me directly you tell me what is your kid  passionate about what do they love to do  and we'll either connect them with a  private instructor to give private  lessons you can join our programming at  show creator studios whatever it is you  want to do we will make it happen for  you i love that okay how are you funded  i know this stuff isn't free so how are  you funded and how can we help you stay  funded oh my gosh thank you we do have  some outstanding supporters here in the  community the engelsted foundation bank  of america envy energy home lights  play studios and then a wonderful  individual donors as well if you just  want to go to the website there's a  floating support button you can click  right there and help these kids  actualize their dreams well let me tell  you i am excited because one of my  dreams came true today because i got to  interview a disney princess oh my  goodness  thank you i am interviewed by the queen  the princess and the queen together  i love it you are awesome my friend if  somebody wants to give you a call what's  the best phone number to reach out to  you you call me personally  407-928-7995 and i want to hear all  about your family your kids and how we  can build that confidence in your child  okay folks yeah and don't forget to  catch us we're going to do the replay on  the mlj facebook live show tonight at 7  pm

